  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Sometimes a chain of physbones is designed so that you're meant to grab the final bone, but trying to grab it tends to grab a previous one in the chain instead.   However, you still want the earlier bones to respond to *collisions*, just not grab attempts.\n\nI'm undecided if this would be best resolved by:\n\n- having a setting so that only the final bone in a chain is grabbable (seems like that would be favorable for performance too?)\n\n- having two different radii for collision radius and grab radius\n\nbut either way would probably work fine.",
